docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2781:Alex explicitly asked to deeply restructure the existing prompt after reading decisions, PRD and prior failures, then measure the effect. This authorizes a new isolated fourth-step prompt arm after D221 failed, not a production default, new storage layer, retrieval change, or full-pipeline run. The [registered design](research/2026-10-29-prompt-restructure/design.md) separates reading the whole current source, deciding the strength and limits of each claim, comparing history, and choosing a research action. D201's independent investment judgement remains the new-question threshold; D202–204's preservation and source-identity rules remain. D221's use-relative standard and D220's necessary-meaning standard are unchanged. Whole-prompt restructuring is one experimental configuration; sentence-level causal attribution is not claimed. Six known development sources plus two historical regression cases are sent three times per arm with the same schema constraints, payload, Haiku model and 6000-token ceiling; the treatment also orders evidence fields before action, within the existing $0.60 cap including two diagnostic continuations. All raw answers are read and recorded, including failures.
